.SH "Detailed Description"
.PP 
Things used for handling physics simulation\&. 

\fBPhysicsBody\fP controls motion, forces and material properties; \fBCollider\fP supplies collision geometry and contact events, and \fBPhysicsConstraint\fP connects bodies\&. Sprites and Parts share these APIs\&.

.PP
\fBNote\fP
.RS 4
Animation physics requires Chipmunk in C++ and JavaScript\&. The Basic solver supports simple shared PhysicsBody/PhysicsConstraint use; it is not an animation-rig backend and will not be expanded to support complex animation physics\&. Use supportsAnimationPhysics() to check build capability and enable Chipmunk on the \fBSpriteLayer\fP before setupAnimationPhysics() or setupPhysicsFromAnimationRig()\&. Ordinary authored playback and pose IK do not require physics\&.
.RE
.PP
.SH "Basic and Chipmunk solver comparison"
.PP
Compare the native solvers using the same physical inputs\&. Step time measures CPU cost; overlap, joint error and settling describe the resulting physical behavior\&. The measurements below apply to the native engine used by both language APIs; they do not measure JavaScript binding or callback overhead\&.

.PP
Latest measurements with all implemented improvements, \fB2,000 dynamic bodies and colliders\fP per test\&. Stack and pile tests add static supports; chains add static anchors\&.

.PP
\fBMean time per simulation step, in milliseconds\&. Lower is faster\&.\fP Each step advances 0\&.01 simulated seconds\&.

.PP
Test  Owner  Basic  Chipmunk  Chipmunk with sleeping  Approaching circle pairs  \fBSprite\fP  0\&.536  0\&.789  —  Approaching circle pairs  \fBPart\fP  0\&.540  0\&.749  —  Touching pairs with angled forces  \fBSprite\fP  0\&.566  0\&.818  —  Touching pairs with angled forces  \fBPart\fP  0\&.561  0\&.765  —  Stacks of 10 boxes  \fBSprite\fP  1\&.559  2\&.346  1\&.499  Stacks of 10 boxes  \fBPart\fP  1\&.469  2\&.218  1\&.010  Chains of 10 pivoted links  \fBSprite\fP  1\&.200  1\&.805  1\&.720  Chains of 10 pivoted links  \fBPart\fP  1\&.125  1\&.632  1\&.701  Piles of 40 boxes  \fBSprite\fP  2\&.953  2\&.292  1\&.421  Piles of 40 boxes  \fBPart\fP  3\&.091  2\&.211  1\&.389  

.PP
Basic and the main Chipmunk column keep all bodies awake\&. The last column enables Chipmunk sleeping after 0\&.5 seconds of inactivity; its timing includes the initial awake period\&. All 2,000 stack and pile bodies eventually slept\&. No chain bodies slept\&. “—” means sleeping was not tested for that workload\&.

.PP
The approach grid varies vertical offset by row and first-contact time from 10 to 1 seconds by column\&. Both solvers hit all 830 intended pairs and avoid all 170 misses, with at most 0\&.01 seconds of contact-time error\&. The touching grid varies force direction from inward to vertical and magnitude from 0\&.5 to 8; both solvers release 995 pairs and keep the five head-on pairs under force\&.

.PP
\fBPhysical accuracy and settling, with sleeping disabled\&.\fP Errors are maximum world distances at the end of the run; lower is better\&. Boxes are 2 units wide\&. Settling times include warmup; “Unsettled” means the scene had not settled by 21\&.2 simulated seconds\&.

.PP
Test  Owner  Error measured  Basic error  Chipmunk error  Basic settled at  Chipmunk settled at  Stacks of 10 boxes  \fBSprite\fP  Box overlap  0\&.790635  0\&.001428  Unsettled  6\&.50 s  Stacks of 10 boxes  \fBPart\fP  Box overlap  0\&.790635  0\&.001296  Unsettled  1\&.20 s  Chains of 10 pivoted links  \fBSprite\fP  Joint anchor separation  0\&.046692  0\&.000002  Unsettled  Unsettled  Chains of 10 pivoted links  \fBPart\fP  Joint anchor separation  0\&.046692  0\&.000002  Unsettled  Unsettled  Piles of 40 boxes  \fBSprite\fP  Box overlap  0\&.897555  0\&.096559  Unsettled  11\&.93 s  Piles of 40 boxes  \fBPart\fP  Box overlap  0\&.965468  0\&.097151  Unsettled  10\&.82 s  

.PP
Settling requires every body below 0\&.05 units/second and 0\&.05 radians/second for a full simulated second\&. No bodies escaped their test areas\&.

.PP
\fBMeasurement setup:\fP Apple M5 Max, 48 GiB RAM, macOS arm64; optimized native engine, contact listeners enabled, no rendering or JavaScript\&. Chipmunk uses the default bounding-box tree and 10 solver iterations\&. All tests use 120 warmup steps\&. Circle results are medians of three run means over 2,000 measured steps; stack, chain and pile results each use one run of 2,000 measured steps\&. Small timing differences in the single-run tests should not be treated as conclusive\&. Measured 2026-09-22\&.
.SH "Watch the solvers side by side"
.PP
This viewer replays recorded runs of the actual C++ solvers\&. Each run simulates 2,000 dynamic bodies; a representative sample is displayed so individual contacts and joints remain visible\&. Both views use the same scale and simulation time\&. Playback speed is independent of the CPU timings above\&. No server, engine build or internet connection is needed after downloading the documentation\&.

.PP
Select approaching circles, touching circles with opposing forces, box stacks, joint chains or box piles\&. Switch between \fBSprite\fP and \fBPart\fP owners, enable Chipmunk sleeping for the box and chain scenes, or pause, scrub, step and slow playback\&. In the circle grids, rows vary offset or force direction and columns increase speed or force\&. Yellow arrows disappear when the touching pair's forces stop\&.

.PP
 
.SH "Class Documentation"
.PP 
.SH "struct pdg::ColliderContact"
.PP 
\fBColliderContact\fP\&. 

One shape contact delivered as eventType_ColliderContact\&.

.PP
\fBNote\fP
.RS 4
Documentation-only JavaScript shape, not a runtime constructor\&.
.RE
.PP
 
.PP
\fBFields\fP
.RS 4
Field  Type  Required/default  Meaning  collider  \fR\fBCollider\fP\fP  Required  impulse  \fR\fBVector\fP\fP  Required  normal  \fR\fBVector\fP\fP  Required  other  \fR\fBCollider\fP\fP  Required  otherShape  \fRnumber\fP  Required  penetration  \fRnumber\fP  Required  phase  \fRnumber\fP  Required  point  \fR\fBPoint\fP\fP  Required  sensor  \fRboolean\fP  Required  shape  \fRnumber\fP  Required  
.RE
.PP
Enable \fBCollider::setWantsContactEvents()\fP on each collider whose owner should receive notifications\&. Both \fBSprite\fP and \fBPart\fP colliders deliver through the owning \fBSprite\fP\&. Each receiving collider sees itself as \fR\fBcollider\fP\fP; vectors reverse for the other endpoint\&. Delivery occurs synchronously after the solve\&.

.PP

.PP
\fBContact fields\fP
.RS 4

.RE
.PP
Field  Meaning  emitter  Owning \fBSprite\fP receiving this event  eventType  \fBpdg::eventType_ColliderContact\fP  collider, other  Shared \fBCollider\fP handles identifying both endpoints  shape, otherShape  Stable shape IDs within the corresponding colliders  phase  collision_Begin, collision_Stay or collision_End  point  Approximate contact \fBPoint\fP in owning-layer/world coordinates  normal  Unit \fBVector\fP directed from collider toward other  impulse  Actual impulse applied to other; zero for sensors, sleeping contacts and end contacts  penetration  Nonnegative overlap depth; zero for an end contact  sensor  Whether either collider is a sensor  

.PP

.PP
Chipmunk contacts reuse its solved manifold: point is the mean of the contact midpoints and penetration is the greatest overlap depth\&. Sleeping pairs continue to report collision_Stay without a new impulse\&.

.PP
Geometry, filters and physical associations are evaluated for the solved frame\&. A callback can remove an endpoint before another notification is delivered; retained handles remain safe and isAttached() reports their current state\&. Contact identity is per shape pair, so compound geometry can generate several notifications for the same two owners\&. Native \fBColliderContact\fP pointers are borrowed only for the callback; JavaScript retains its \fBCollider\fP handles\&. 
.PP
